{"v":1,"st":"OK","e":"2024-11-05","src":{"clerk-statistics-2024":["Office of the Clerk, U.S. House of Representatives: Statistics of the Presidential and Congressional Election of November 5, 2024","https://clerk.house.gov/member_info/electionInfo/2024/statistics2024.pdf","official",1,"2026-10-24","d4ba800fc17135b616ae556c92861080ab962d95916ace34b546c5aac824aec4",0],"county-export":["Oklahoma State Election Board, results site, Export: 'County Level Results - CSV (Zipped)'","https://results.okelections.us/OKER/?elecDate=20241105","official",1,"2026-10-03","f3a8370a49385910c825b01006ce33bcf6fc0c18b796cf01188ae2caa1e4527b",1]},"notes":["Compiled by the Clerk from official sources; Oklahoma's section begins on page 57 of the PDF. Compared with the Board's files for every federal contest; the totals of the 2024 House contests.","The Board's own results file for the general election of 11/5/2024, from the Export menu of its results page, which was marked 'Official Results' when the file was saved through a browser on 2026-10-03 (this is that copy: its SHA-256 is the one recorded then). The results site refuses scripts, so nothing is asked of it here. The county election boards certify their counties' results; the State Election Board certifies the federal, state, legislative and judicial contests and the state questions. Listed on https://oklahoma.gov/elections/elections-results/election-results/2024-election-results/november-general-election.html."],"gaps":[["state","The State Election Board's certified summary of November 2024","The Board's archive lists an agenda and minutes for its certification meeting of 12 November 2024 but no meeting packet, and both are scans, so no certified summary of the 2024 figures can be read. The federal contests are compared with the Clerk of the House's statistics; every other 2024 contest rests on the Board's own precinct and county results files agreeing with each other, and carries no separate certified total.","https://oklahoma.gov/elections/about-us/meeting-notices-agendas-and-minutes-archives/2024-agendas-and-minutes.html"],["state","Offices with no contest","Oklahoma prints a race on the November ballot only when it is contested (the Clerk of the House's statistics: 'According to Oklahoma law, the names of those with no opposition are not printed on the ballot'), so a candidate unopposed at filing, or elected outright in the June primary or the August runoff, has no November result here.","https://oklahoma.gov/elections/elections-results/election-results/2024-election-results/november-general-election.html"],["state","City, town and school board elections held at other times","Most Oklahoma city, town and school board elections are held in the spring, not in November; only the city, town, school and fire district contests and questions that were on this November ballot are here.","https://oklahoma.gov/elections/elections-results/election-results/2024-election-results/november-general-election.html"]],"chk":{"n":12,"ok":12,"not":[]},"cty":{"40001":"Adair County","40003":"Alfalfa County","40005":"Atoka County","40007":"Beaver County","40009":"Beckham County","40011":"Blaine County","40013":"Bryan County","40015":"Caddo County","40017":"Canadian County","40019":"Carter County","40021":"Cherokee County","40023":"Choctaw County","40025":"Cimarron County","40027":"Cleveland County","40029":"Coal County","40031":"Comanche County","40033":"Cotton County","40035":"Craig County","40037":"Creek County","40039":"Custer County","40041":"Delaware County","40043":"Dewey County","40045":"Ellis County","40047":"Garfield County","40049":"Garvin County","40051":"Grady County","40053":"Grant County","40055":"Greer County","40057":"Harmon County","40059":"Harper County","40061":"Haskell County","40063":"Hughes County","40065":"Jackson County","40067":"Jefferson County","40069":"Johnston County","40071":"Kay County","40073":"Kingfisher County","40075":"Kiowa County","40077":"Latimer County","40079":"Le Flore Cou